# Cursor rules — {{.Name}}
# Generated by forge new langchain-agents (forge {{.ForgeVer}})

## Project type
Multi-agent Python system using LangGraph, LangChain, LangServe, and LangSmith.

## What to do

- When adding a new agent: create `src/agents/<name>.py`, register in `src/graph/workflow.py`,
  and generate tests in `tests/test_<name>.py` and `tests/security/test_<name>_injection.py`.
- When adding a new tool: create `src/tools/<name>.py`, implement as a `@tool` or `BaseTool` subclass.
- When modifying `AgentState`: update `src/graph/state.py` and check all nodes that read/write the changed key.
- After any change to prompts or system messages: run `forge scan prompt-injection`.

## What NOT to do

- Do NOT hardcode API keys, model names, or URLs — use `src/shared/config.py`.
- Do NOT use `print()` in non-test code — use `structlog.get_logger()`.
- Do NOT use `float` for costs or budgets — use `Decimal`.
- Do NOT make blocking IO calls inside async agent nodes.
- Do NOT share state between agents via global variables.
- Do NOT call `os.exit()` inside agent nodes — raise a typed `AgentError` instead.

## File naming conventions

| Artefact | Path |
|---|---|
| Agent | `src/agents/<name>.py` |
| Tool | `src/tools/<name>.py` |
| Graph node | `src/graph/workflow.py` |
| State | `src/graph/state.py` |
| Unit test | `tests/test_<name>.py` |
| Injection test | `tests/security/test_<name>_injection.py` |
| Migration | `migrations/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_<description>.sql` |
